<Item XName="Note" UserName="Note" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 1.2pt 0in; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;B&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 18pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 11.0pt&quot;&gt;V5G&amp;nbsp;Downlink Throughput&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;H2 class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/H2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 12pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;,&apos;serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;This&amp;nbsp;workspace demonstrates complete link-level V5G (Verizon &lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;5G)&amp;nbsp;downlink shared channel transmission, which&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;comprises of complete source, channel and receiver.&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: &apos;Arial&apos;,&apos;sans-serif&apos;; mso-fareast-font-family: &apos;Times New Roman&apos;&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Supported Features:&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;1. Complete xPDSCH physical layer simulation, including digital baseband source, digital baseband receiver, analog source, analog receiver and channel.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2. Simplified&amp;nbsp;channel model for beamforming evaluation, which is a revision of delay-scaled CDL model (please refer to TR38.900).&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;2. BRS configurations &quot;One Slot&quot; and &quot;One Subframe&quot; are supported.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 3. PRACH configurations #0 and #1 ae supported.&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Included Designs&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/STRONG&gt;1. SISO: 1-layer transmission in complete V5G&amp;nbsp;DL shared channel&amp;nbsp;simulation with hybrid beamformin&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 2. MIMO: 2-layer transmission, hybrid beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 3. SISO Baseline: 1-layer transmission, no beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 4. SIMO_RxDiversity: two branches are selected dynamically, hybrid beamforming&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 5. SIMO_RxDiversityRxAntennaElementPattern: four RFICs are configured in RX side for diversity receiving.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 5. SISO_EMProRxBeamPattern; beam pattern files for RX side generated by EMPro are included in the simulation&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 6. SISO_EMProTxRxBeamPattern: beam pattern files for both RX side and TX side generated by EMPro are included in the simulation&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 7. SISO_DFRF: RF part design is included&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 8. SISO_2UserTx_1UserRev: 2 users are configured in the source and one of them can be chosen to analyze the performance&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;UL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Notes:&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; &lt;/STRONG&gt;1. UPA (Uniform Planer Array) is applied to TX&amp;nbsp;side, so number of antennas in Y-axis and number of antennas in Z-axis should be specified in TX. In RX side, there are different&amp;nbsp;antenna array configuration approaches. In designs without beam pattern importing, UPA is applied, but in others, RX antenna array topology is implicitly included in&amp;nbsp;EMPro, HFSS and CST files.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 2. Regarding&amp;nbsp;the simplified&amp;nbsp;channel modeling,&amp;nbsp;section 7.7.1 of 3GPP TR38.901 says &quot;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB&gt;&lt;FONT size=2 face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt;For modeling effect of beamforming in a simplified way, a brick-wall window can be applied to a delay-scaled CDL model. The power shall be normalized after applying the window.&lt;/FONT&gt;&quot;,&lt;FONT face=Arial&gt; but&amp;nbsp;it does propose any approach to implement the simplified model. In&amp;nbsp;our 3D channel model, there is a parameter named &quot;UseOneRayPerCluster&quot;.&amp;nbsp;If&amp;nbsp;it&apos;s enabled,&amp;nbsp;only one ray is modeled for each cluster. The approach has already been&amp;nbsp;verified in our previous 5G library. Both MIMO design and SISO design&amp;nbsp;enable &quot;UseOneRayPerCluster&quot; for beamforming evaluation.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 3.&amp;nbsp;To get reasonable performance curve in simulation, TX/RX sweeping beams and channels&apos; AoA/ZoA/AoD/ZoD need predefined carefully. For&amp;nbsp;example, if AoA = [30], ZoA = [90],&amp;nbsp;AoD = [315] and ZoD = [75]&amp;nbsp;are the channel parameters, the channel directions&amp;nbsp;would better&amp;nbsp;be&amp;nbsp;the member&amp;nbsp;of corresponding TX and RX sweeping beams.&lt;BR&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 4. Only one user is supported in RX side, while multiple users are supported to configure&amp;nbsp;in source. SISO_2UserTx_1UserRev demoes the case, where multipler users can be configured in the source and user of interest can be specified in the receiver for receiving.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 5. xPDCCH is not included for demodulation, although &quot;SearchSpaceIndex&quot; as a xPDCCH-related parameter appears in the parameter page of the schematic and xPBCH, ePBCH and CSI-RS are also precluded&amp;nbsp;currently.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 6. EVM, BER&amp;nbsp;and Throughput/BLER can be analyzed.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 7. Beam pattern can be shown dynamically, while it will slow down the simulation speed heavily.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 8. The output buswidth of TX basedband source can be set to 1~16 upon the paramter NumTxPorts in V5G_DL_Src model. For data transmission, if there are multiple ports, the first port is mapped to the first&amp;nbsp;line of the maximum 16-width bus, the second port is mapped to the second line of the 16-width bus, and so on.&amp;nbsp;For example, given NumBRSPorts = 8 and AP_Layer_Config = 6, then the first 8 ports of the&amp;nbsp;16-width bus will be used to transmit BRS and the first and&amp;nbsp;fifth ports of the 16-width bus will be used to transmit xPDSCH.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 9. MCS = 3&amp;nbsp;is configured in most of the reference designs, where&amp;nbsp;the system will&amp;nbsp;run in low SNR range&amp;nbsp;in SISO case (around 1~1.5 dB).&amp;nbsp;The performance curve for SISO is evaluated&amp;nbsp;in terms of&amp;nbsp;SNR&amp;nbsp;subtracting beamforming gain named &quot;BFGain_Expected&quot; in the equation page of the schematic (in some design, BFGain_Expected may be splitted into TxBFGain_Expected and RxBFGain_Expected). For&amp;nbsp;other MCS configurations, please refer to section 8.1.5.1 of V5G_213_v1.4. Briefly,&amp;nbsp;QPSK is applied in MCS range [0, 5], 16QAM is applied in MCS range [6, 10] and 64QAM is applied in MCS range [11, 14].&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 10. If too&amp;nbsp;small SNR is set, the synchronization may fail in some cases.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;11.&amp;nbsp;&quot;Perf_MCS11&quot; and &quot;Perf_MCS3&quot; are added to show&amp;nbsp;performance comparison between baseline and system with BF under MCS=3, as well as&amp;nbsp;between HARQ is on and off under MCS=3 and MCS=11. Obviously, when MCS=11, operating SNR is around 14dB.&amp;nbsp;It shows HARQ-on outperforms HARQ-off in all SNR range under MCS=11, but story is different when MCS=3. The intersection in &quot;Perf_MCS3&quot; is caused by TX beam index&amp;nbsp;report error. Since TX Beam Index is updated every 25 subframes, once there is a TX Beam Index report error, the following 25 subframes&amp;nbsp;are definitely lost and what&apos;s more,&amp;nbsp;the combination among the first failed transmission and following upto three transmission is useless for following decoding. It seems in a real system, BSI need filtered&amp;nbsp;before use.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 12. SISO_DFRF design imports more realistic&amp;nbsp;RF modeling into simulation, where impairments can be introduced easily.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 13.&amp;nbsp;Co-sim of SystemVue and&amp;nbsp;pattern files generated by EMPro, HFSS and CST is a hot topic.&amp;nbsp;Hereby, multiple co-sim approaches are provided for reference.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; All these kinds of simulation depend on pattern files and we take pattern files generated by EMPro as example.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; Three designs are related to co-sim: SIMO_RxDiversityRxAntennaElementPattern, SISO_EMProRxBeamPattern and SISOProTxRxBeamPattern.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; SIMO_RxDiversityRxAntennaElementPattern uses&amp;nbsp;RFIC#1, RFIC#2, RFIC#3 and RFIC#4, each of which is consititued of two elements. The&amp;nbsp;elements&apos; pattern files of RFIC # are RFIC#_elements_001.uan and RFIC#_elements_002.uan. In the design&amp;nbsp;the phase and topology informaion are included in the pattern files.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; SISO_EMProRxBeamPattern&amp;nbsp;and SISOProTxRxBeamPattern&amp;nbsp;demo another more efficient and more realistic&amp;nbsp;way to do simulation in Massive MIMO scenario. They import&amp;nbsp;synthesized&amp;nbsp;beam pattern files, but not antenna&amp;nbsp;element files in simulation. There are seven beam pattern files for TX, namely TxArray001_001.uan ~ TxArray001_007.uan and four beam pattern files for RX,&amp;nbsp;namely RxArray001_001.uan ~ RxArray001_004.uan.&amp;nbsp;Please notice that beam pattern files&amp;nbsp;are different from antenna element pattern files. Antenna element pattern files only&amp;nbsp;characterrize&amp;nbsp;the radiation of each element, rather, beam pattern files describe synthesized beam radiation with sharp beam in specific directions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; SISO_EMProRxBeamPattern only applies beam pattern files in RX side, but SISOProTxRxBeamPattern applies beam pattern files&amp;nbsp;in both TX and RX side.&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;By virtue of the introduction of beam pattern files in simulation, for a 1-layer transmission, channel model only needs to model a 1-by-1 channel regarding how many elements there are, which speed up Massive MIMO dramatically.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;&lt;BR&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp; 14. AP_Layer_Config follows &lt;BR&gt;&lt;/DIV&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;DIV class=MsoNormal style=&quot;MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: normal&quot; align=center&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;TABLE class=MsoNormalTable style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-yfti-tbllook: 1184; mso-padding-alt: 0in 5.4pt 0in 5.4pt; mso-border-insideh: .5pt solid windowtext; mso-border-insidev: .5pt solid windowtext&quot; cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 border=1&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;TBODY&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;TR style=&quot;mso-yfti-irow: 0; mso-yfti-firstrow: yes&quot;&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;TD style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: windowtext 1pt solid; BORDER-RIGHT: windowtext 1pt solid; WIDTH: 106.1pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; BORDER-LEFT: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt&quot; vAlign=top width=141&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&apos;mso-fareast-font-family: &quot;Malgun Gothic&quot;; mso-fareast-language: KO&apos;&gt;&lt;FONT size=2&gt;Value&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/TD&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;TD style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: windowtext 1pt solid; BORDER-RIGHT: windowtext 1pt solid; WIDTH: 276.6pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0in; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; BORDER-LEFT: #f0f0f0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-border-left-alt: solid windowtext .5pt&quot; vAlign=top width=369&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in